      "a": "During sexual reproduction, both male and female parents contribute equally to the child. Each progeny trait is determined by a pair of alleles, and male and female gametes each have one allele. During fertilisation, each allele pair combines to determine phenotypes. As a result, child qualities are decided by equal genes from both male and female parents."
